{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "declaration": false,
    "declarationMap": false,
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "rootDir": "../..",
    // ESNext, not the ES2022 this pinned until 2026-08-28. `tsconfig.json`
    // already compiles this same source with the base config's `lib: ESNext`,
    // so the narrower floor here was checking against a target the package
    // never ships to — and it cost three phantom errors on a `findLastIndex`
    // in host code the tests pull in.
    "lib": ["ESNext", "DOM"],
    "types": ["bun", "node"],
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    // The same mapping `server-core`, `server`, `shared`, `apps/cli`,
    // `apps/electron` and `apps/webui` already carry. Needed HERE because
    // `rootDir` is the repo root and the test files below deliberately import
    // host code (`spawner-budget-cap.test.ts` pins `HOST_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED_ERROR`
    // against server-core's copy, which `spawner.ts` re-declares rather than
    // imports so the host stays out of the Pi bundle). Without it, server-core's
    // `@nessy-agent/shared/<subpath>` imports — legal under its own tsconfig,
    // absent from shared's `exports` map — fail to resolve, and 203 cascading
    // errors get attributed to a package that is green in the chain.
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@nessy-agent/shared": ["../shared/src/index.ts"],
      "@nessy-agent/shared/*": ["../shared/src/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"],
  // Until 2026-08-28 this was the single glob `**/*.test.ts`, which took all 85
  // test files out of the program in one line and swallowed every new one for
  // free. Measured that day with the glob removed: 423 errors — 206 of them in
  // `server-core`, i.e. not this package's at all and gone once `paths`/`lib`
  // above were fixed. The residue measured that day was 217 errors in 32 files;
  // the other 53 test files typecheck clean and are now in the program, as is
  // every test file added from here on.
  //
  // This list may only shrink. `scripts/check-typecheck-coverage.ts` caps it and
  // rejects a glob, so the one-line version cannot come back.
  //
  // 2026-08-28, P3.165: the 27-error `TextContent | ImageContent` cluster is
  // GONE — all 27 were unnarrowed `content[0]?.text` reads on a discriminated
  // union, in four files whose tools emit only `type: 'text'`, so every one was
  // real drift and none was a test pinning removed behaviour. Fixed with
  // `src/__tests__/support/tool-result-text.ts`, which THROWS on a non-text
  // part rather than casting or substituting `''` — two of the 27 were negative
  // assertions that the `''` substitution would have satisfied vacuously.
  // `ask-user-tool`, `subagent-tool` and `notebook` cleared entirely and are off
  // this list; 190 remain in the 29 files below.
  //
  // 2026-08-28, P3.165 second pass: the seven single-error files and the five
  // files whose ONLY errors were arity are gone too — 29 files to 19, 190
  // errors to 172. The arity fix was applied ONLY where it is provably
  // runtime-neutral: `ToolDefinition.execute` requires five positional
  // parameters and `src/tools/notebook.ts:125` is the ONLY implementation in
  // this package that declares the fifth (`ctx`), so for every call site
  // touched the added `undefined, {} as never` cannot reach a reader.
  //
  // `onupdate-stream.test.ts` was NOT a typing repair: its `runAgentLoop` call
  // omitted the required `signal` and `streamFn`, and the test had been FAILING
  // at runtime with "No default stream function configured" — the exclusion hid
  // the type error naming the cause. It passes now.
  //
  // Third pass, same day: five more cleared — the three `*-real-server` files
  // guarded on the KEY (`'toolCall' in next`) where the array's two differently
  // shaped literals make TS carry each other's key as optional-undefined, so
  // the guard never eliminated `undefined`; and the two search-provider files
  // had zero-arg `fetch` stubs where their own siblings in the same file
  // declare the parameter list. 172 to 159, 19 files to 14.
  //
  // What is left is 159 errors in the 14 files below, and it is no longer one
  // shape — 79 `TS2554` remain but every one sits in a file carrying other
  // errors too, so clearing arity alone no longer shortens this list. Read the
  // arity note above before touching them: the `undefined, {} as never` fix is
  // only sound because `src/tools/notebook.ts:125` is the sole implementation
  // declaring a fifth parameter, and that proof has to be redone per target.
  //
  // The reductions from here are per-file: `workflow-tool` (45),
  // `create-search-tool` (17), `tool-wrapper` (17), `pi-runtime-adapter` (13).
  // Two fixture shapes recur across them and are worth reading once rather than
  // fixing twenty times: fixtures missing `environmentProfile`/`environmentDigest`
  // (which `SupervisedProcessResult` grew — see `background-bash.test.ts`), and
  // `PiChildSessionPort` fixtures missing `sealOwnerTask`.
  //
  // P6.819, 2026-09-08: `pi-harness-baseline.test.ts` is OFF this list — its 18
  // errors are fixed and it is now in the program, so the file the whole harness
  // contract rests on is compiled by `typecheck:pi-agent-server` rather than by
  // nothing. Both recurring fixture shapes above were two of its four causes;
  // the other two were bun's `expect(any, any)` resolving to
  // `Matchers<undefined>` and a `WorkflowRuntimeApi` literal carrying a `child`
  // member the sandbox has never bound.
  //
  // Fourth pass (P3.249): `guardian-runner.test.ts` cleared — 14 files to 13.
  // Two errors, both the same shape and neither the arity one: three
  // `{ id, name, shortName }` literals standing in for a full
  // `ModelDefinition`, replaced by one `gatewayModel()` helper. Cleared
  // BECAUSE the row was adding tests to that file and an excluded test file is
  // not typechecked at all — `bun run typecheck:all` would have passed over a
  // new `runtimeDefinitions` fixture missing two required fields, which is
  // exactly what it did until this line moved.
  //
  // P3.198, measured 2026-09-03 — and the measurement CORRECTS the row it closes.
  //
  // The row generalised from one instance: an excluded test file was red at
  // RUNTIME because the exclusion hid the type error naming the cause
  // (`onupdate-stream.test.ts`, calling `runAgentLoop` with 4 of 6 required
  // arguments). It concluded the thirteen below are "an unknown mixture of
  // drift and dead tests" and that each may have been silently broken for
  // months. Run, they are not that.
  //
  // All thirteen, under `bun test` at load ~12: 174 tests, **171 pass, 3 fail**,
  // 6.50 s. Every failure is in ONE file, `pi-harness-baseline.test.ts`, and
  // every one is a pin that a landed commit moved without moving the pin:
  //
  //   - `NessyMcpClient.prototype` gained `getInstructions` in `6acef70b7`
  //     ("every runtime dropped the half of a server's introduction that is not
  //     a tool name"); the prototype list in that test still spells twelve names.
  //   - `SESSION_TOOLS_REQUIRING_HOST_CALLBACK` gained `list_sessions` and
  //     `get_session_info` in `c197a8bb4` (P3.222); the fixture's
  //     `availabilityAudit.hostCallbackExcludedNames` still spells 31.
  //   - The compact-ordering marker `const result = await handle.compact(
  //     msg.customInstructions)` became a multi-line call in `413354e4b`
  //     (project compaction steering); the ordered-marker list still matches the
  //     single-line text.
  //
  // So the mechanism is NOT this exclusion. A pin comparing two runtime values
  // is red under `bun test` whether or not the compiler ever saw the file — and
  // `bun test` is the command CI runs and no lane runs in its implementation
  // loop, which is P2.255's seam, not P3.156's. The exclusion's own cost is the
  // narrower one the row started from: a type error that WOULD have named the
  // cause is not reported here, so when such a test does break, it breaks
  // silently and without a diagnosis.
  //
  // Read together, the two say the same thing about this list from opposite
  // sides: a file on it is checked by exactly one command, and that command is
  // the one nobody runs. Three pins were stale on the day this was written and
  // the tree was green for every lane that touched them.
  //
  // A fourth failure appeared and disappeared during the same measurement — the
  // `agent.subagent` source-state digest — and it was a NEIGHBOURING LANE'S
  // uncommitted edit to `orchestrator/subagent-tool.ts`, not drift. Anything
  // measured over a working tree during a parallel wave needs that check before
  // it is recorded; `check:surface` printed `6/6 match live source` twenty
  // minutes before printing the same pin as DRIFT.
  //
  // F1.1297, 2026-10-09: `pi-runtime-adapter.test.ts` is OFF this list — its 13
  // errors are fixed and the file is in the program. Twelve were the doubles
  // owing their real signatures: `streamFn` on the one direct `new Agent` (the
  // run had always used the SDK's module-load default, `streamSimple`),
  // `ToolExecutionRequest` on a toolExecutor member, the optional
  // `extensionFactories` spread, `unknown` on two fakeSession override
  // parameters, `ToolDefinition` on a registerTool parameter, five non-null
  // asserts on the recorded loader options, and a `never` cast where a full
  // `AgentSession` matcher met the partial double. The thirteenth was the only
  // real drift, exactly the shape P3.198 predicted: the compact fixture
  // answered a `{ ok: true }` the runtime never had — it now returns the SDK's
  // own `CompactionResult`, so the delegation test pins the summary /
  // firstKeptEntryId / tokensBefore shape the host reads. Twelve entries to
  // eleven.
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "src/extensions/closed-host.test.ts",
    "src/extensions/deferred-mcp-extension.test.ts",
    "src/extensions/lifecycle-bridge.test.ts",
    "src/harness/tool-manifest.test.ts",
    "src/local-tools/tool-wrapper.test.ts",
    "src/nessy-metadata-schema.test.ts",
    "src/orchestrator/review-tool.test.ts",
    "src/orchestrator/workflow-tool.test.ts",
    "src/package-manifest.test.ts",
    "src/session-tool-registration.test.ts",
    "src/tools/search/create-search-tool.test.ts"
  ]
}
